        "value": 1
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "Looks like the core city is back up to speed. It didn't stop for long."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "On the upside, that should have been Reunion taking in a group of Infected migrants from Lungmen. I hope..."
    },
    {
        "command": "character",
        "params": {
            "name": "char_003_kalts_1"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "But we may have to change up our strategy."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "We can expect the city to make a few more stops along the way until the enemy commander decides to announce her plan. Then she'll stop taking in Infected refugees."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "At that time, should Wei Yenwu decide to attack, the enemy will redeploy their defensive units. We may be exposed in the process, and come under attack."
    },
    {
        "command": "character",
        "params": {
            "name": "char_003_kalts_1",
            "name2": "char_002_amiya_1",
            "focus": 2
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "I hope our agreement with Miss Fumizuki will buy us some time from Chief Wei..."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "Hm.. we're already very close to the center of the core city."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "There are a lot of passages above and below us that seem like they were part of the city's transit system. After the Catastrophe, everything stopped working."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "That does mean it's impossible for the city to function, and even move...? Could this be the underground structure Dr. Kal'tsit was talking about?"
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "Regardless, these passages make good cover for us. The number of enemy guards has nearly doubled in this storage area close to the central district..."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Amiya",
        "text": "We haven't seen much resistance since entering the core city. But once we proceed to the central district, we should expect to run into a lot more Reunion forces."
    },
    {
        "command": "character",
        "params": {
            "name": "char_003_kalts_1"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "The recon and spec ops teams are already in position. So far so good."
    },
    {
        "command": "decision",
        "params": {
            "options": "Why do we only have three teams working together?",
            "values": "1"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "predicate",
        "params": {
            "references": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "character",
        "params": {
            "name": "char_003_kalts_1"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "The recon and spec ops teams both have their own missions."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Raidian is leading the recon team for this operation, as one of Rhodes Island's communications specialists."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Thanks to Raidian, the recon team serves as the focal point for our comms in this operation."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Even here in the core city, we'll be able to communicate with the other teams. That's because of their hard work."
    },
    {
        "command": "decision",
        "params": {
            "options": "I didn't see them...",
            "values": "1"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "predicate",
        "params": {
            "references": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "The recon team always works alone."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Outcast, Raidian, and Scout, who heroically gave his life in the Chernobog rescue mission\u2014"
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "The elite operators leading the recon teams are responsible for leading their squads alone, identifying and reporting threats, and attempting to resolve them without assistance."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Raidian isn't as skilled in combat as the other two elite operators, but she is a unique talent at Rhodes Island when it comes to directly influencing the course of a battle."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "We've got three teams engaging in this assault operation. We don't need Raidian to trouble herself with combat."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "As for the spec ops team, their mission also avoids direct combat."
    },
    {
        "command": "decision",
        "params": {
            "options": "Explain it to me.;......;So you're not going to tell me what it is?",
            "values": "1;2;3"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "predicate",
        "params": {
            "references": "1;2;3"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "It's enough to know that they're necessary. You'll know the details soon enough."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Each team makes up a link in the chain of our strategy. That stable structure breeds a stable result."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Conversely, a formidable opponent has a tangled and twisted root structure. They pull in nutrients from every level. Hacking off branches does them no harm."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "We have to set their roots alight before they even know we're here."
    },
    {
        "command": "decision",
        "params": {
            "options": "Huh? What are you talking about?;......;I think I get it.",
            "values": "1;2;3"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "predicate",
        "params": {
            "references": "1;2;3"
        }
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "Heh. I'm pretty sure you get it all..."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Kal'tsit",
        "text": "'Doctor.'"
    },
    {
        "command": "dialog"
    },
    {
        "command": "character"
    },
